"Declaration of Address Verification (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/WG-015)\nciteturn1672search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; # Declaration of Address Verification (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) (WG-015) ... This form tells the court when and how you verified the judgment debtor’s address.\n\n# Declaration of Address Verification (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) (WG-015)\n\nIf you are enforcing a judgment for personal debt, you are required to verify the judgment debtor's address no later than 12 months before you give\nthe levying officer any papers to serve on the judgment debtor. This form tells the court when and how you verified the judgment debtor’s address.\n\nGet form WG-015\n\n  * 汉语Get form WG-015 in Chinese Simplified (Chinese Simplified)\n  * 한국어Get form WG-015 in Korean (Korean)\n  * españolGet form WG-015 in Spanish (Spanish)\n\nEffective: July 1, 2026\n\n  * Go to How-to instructions for Debt Collection--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWG-015/EJ-135 (https://courts.ca.gov/documents/wg015.pdf)\nciteturn1672search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago;  | WG-015/EJ-135 FOR COURT USE ONLY ... Judicial Council of California, courts.ca.gov\nWG-015/EJ-135\n | WG-015/EJ-135 FOR COURT USE ONLY\n--- | ---\nSUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF STREET ADDRESS: MAILING ADDRESS: CITY AND ZIP CODE: BRANCH NAME: | WG-015/EJ-135 None\nPLAINTIFF/PETITIONER: DEFENDANT/RESPONDENT: | WG-015/EJ-135 None\nDECLARATION OF ADDRESS VERIFICATION (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) | WG-015/EJ-135 CASE NUMBER:\nInstructions to the judgment creditor for completing this form: If you are enforcing a judgment for personal debt, you are required to verify the judgment debtor's address no later than 12 months before you give the levying officer any papers to serve on the judgment debtor. (Code Civ. Proc., § 684.130.) You must notify the levying officer and the court that you have completed the address verification by completing this form, giving a copy to the levying officer, and filing the completed form with the court within 10 business days of giving a copy to the levying officer. | WG-015/EJ-135 None\n1. I am (specify):\nattorney for\noriginal judgment creditor \nassignee of record\nb.\non (date): \nSending a letter or legal pleading to the judgment debtor's address                                                    using certified mail, or \nthrough some other method of transmission through the United States Postal Service that provides a return receipt, and \nreceived a return receipt signed by the judgment debtor. \nc.\non (date): \nUsing a commercial address verification service, including skip-tracing, or using a public records database. I then sent a \nletter or legal pleading to the verified address via first-class mail                                                    and the letter or legal \npleading was not returned to sender.\nd.\nUsing the following method (describe the method and the date it was completed):\nI declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California that the foregoing is true and correct.\nDate:\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME)\n(SIGNATURE)\nWG-015/EJ-135, Page 1 of 1\nJudicial Council of California, courts.ca.gov \nNew January 1, 2026, Mandatory Form \nCode Civ. Proc., § 684.130\nDeclaration of Address Verification \n(Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment)\nPrint\nSave\nClear\nFor your protection and privacy, please press the Clear \nbutton after you have printed the form.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=1&query=SH-)\nciteturn1672search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * WG-015 * Declaration of Address Verification (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment) Effective: July 1, 2026 汉语 